    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup construction is headlined by the elite-tier output of **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.07). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary target against Lowder; with a favorable park, a soft SP_xERA of 5.25, and a prime #2 slot, he is positioned to capitalize on his elite sprint speed in a high-leverage environment. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** draws a massive boost from a dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) against Burrows, making him a cornerstone of our daily production. We are also banking on **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) and **James Wood** (67.30), who both benefit from aggressive batting order placement and highly favorable pitching matchups that should keep our offensive floor secure.\n\nStrategic deployment of our bench required a difficult decision between **Max Muncy** (57.70) and **Alex Freeland** (45.91). While **Alex Freeland** was under heavy consideration, the optimizer ultimately favored **Max Muncy** due to his projected #8 spot against the LHP Freeland, which offers a significant 10% SP skill bump and a 7% platoon advantage that outweighs the marginal versatility of **Alex Freeland**. We are flagging potential volatility with our \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**; should any be dropped down the order or benched, our offensive floor could fluctuate. Notably, **Jose Caballero** remains a start despite a lukewarm 44.40 score, though we are wary of his sub-par matchup against Gausman and his high-risk profile against elite arms. We are monitoring weather closely, but currently, our starters are cleared for action, provided the official lineups confirm these projected slots.",
